{
  "requirement": "Under {cite}`requirements.cli.skill_structure`, the `habeas` skill MUST be the home of routing tasks to skills, `habeas status` and `habeas info`, directive and reference syntax, distributed requirements, and gotchas common to every task.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed test is adequate for the subject. It covers each home topic the requirement names and checks that no other skill restates them.\n\nThe only test for this requirement is `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_habeas_skill_is_home_of_routing_inspection_syntax_and_shared_gotchas]`. I read the helpers `assert_text`, `section`, `assert_home`, `home_markers`, `assert_phrases` and `bundled_skill`. I also read `assets/skills/habeas/SKILL.md`.\n\nObligations and how the test covers them:\n- **Routing tasks to skills.** `assert_text` checks that the `## Workflow` section of the habeas `SKILL.md` contains the `| Task | Skill |` table header. `assert_home` also asserts that this marker is present in the habeas skill.\n- **`habeas status` and `habeas info`.** The `## Inspecting` section is checked for both command forms. The marker \"A selection is a full name or a glob…\" is also checked in the habeas skill.\n- **Directive and reference syntax.**\n  - The `## Requirements, examples, and definitions` section is checked for the `{req}`, `{example}` and `{definition}` text.\n  - The `## References` section is checked for \"Write a reference with a full name in a comment…\" and \"Fence a reference\".\n  - `references/syntax-details.md` is checked for its \"Full names in nested chapters\" and \"Anchors\" headings.\n  - `home_markers` adds \"Its full name is the chapter path…\" and \"omit a leading `reqs/`…\".\n- **Distributed requirements.** `references/distributed-requirements.md` is checked for its \"# Distributed requirements\" heading. `home_markers` adds the substantive markers \"`:::{violations} <name>` selects constructs likely to break it\" and \"Each site-query match makes a site\". `assert_home` asserts these are present in the habeas skill's `SKILL.md` and `references/` files.\n- **Gotchas common to every task.** The `## Gotchas` section is checked for the Git-index gotcha. `home_markers` adds \"silently defines nothing\" and \"needs a longer outer fence such as `::::{req}`\". It also adds the coverage-artifact and prerequisite statements.\n- **Each topic stated in full in exactly one skill (the parent `requirements.cli.skill_structure` obligation, as it applies to this home).** `assert_home` loops over the other four bundled skills, whose `SKILL.md` and `references/` files `bundled_skill` loads. It asserts that none contains any of the habeas home markers, with a message naming the skill that restates one. A wrong-home or duplicated statement therefore fails the test.\n\nI found no plausible violation that this test would accept. Deleting a topic or moving it to another skill fails either the section or marker assertions, or the non-restatement loop. Cross-skill reference behavior and the other skills' homes belong to sibling requirements and their own tests, so I did not assess them here.",
  "references": "3e613787d62d50092286fd528020c2381ceb86235c44291883f55c4a6d9690e7",
